# pouch — boundary-line patch series against vendored musl 1.2.5.
#
# quilt-style ordered list: one patch file per line, applied top-to-bottom
# from the musl tree root. Lines starting with '#' are comments; blank lines
# are ignored. See README.md in this directory for the discipline.
#
# Invariant P-4 (POUCH-DESIGN.md §11): every patch touches ONLY where musl
# meets the kernel -- the syscall seam and the lower half -- never the portable
# algorithms above it (string / stdlib / math / stdio's formatting and
# buffering core). "stdio" is NOT wholly upper half, whatever this header used
# to say: its fd-facing BACKENDS (__stdio_read/write/close/seek, the openers,
# tmpfile) are lower half, and 0002 / 0023 / 0035 / 0036 / 0038 patch them.
#
# There is no per-directory inventory to review a patch against.
# docs/reference/78-pouch.md, cited here for years, is an absorbed stub and
# never held one. The as-built boundary is DERIVED, not kept:
#   grep -h '^+++ b/' *.patch | cut -d/ -f2-3 | sort | uniq -c
# A patch that adds a directory to that list is a P-4 review event, argued in
# its own header and in the owning dossier (vault/system/boundary/pouch-seam/).
#
# tools/build.sh sysroot copies third_party/musl/ to build/pouch/musl-src/,
# applies the patches below in order, then builds the pouch libc out-of-tree.
# The boundary-line replacement continues across Phase 6 sub-chunks 5-13 —
# see docs/POUCH-DESIGN.md §14.

