0031-pouch-readlink.patch
# 0032: #150 -- honest _SC_NPROCESSORS via /ctl/sched "cpus: N" (the Go
# runtime getCPUCount precedent). The seam ENOSYSes sched_getaffinity, so
# upstream popcounted its {1} seed to 1 forever; llvmpipe/LLVM/nproc all
# saw one CPU. Fail-soft 1.
0032-pouch-sysconf-nprocs.patch
# 0033: B-0 -- pthread_getattr_np() reported a ONE-PAGE main-thread stack
# (upstream probes the extent with mremap, which the seam ENOSYSes). State the
# exec mapping instead: [0x7ff00000, 0x80000000). pouch-hello-threads requires
# the answer to equal the kernel's own /proc/<pid>/maps `stack` row.
0033-pouch-getattr-np-main-stack.patch
# 0034: B-0 -- sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES/_SC_AVPHYS_PAGES) returned UNINITIALISED
# STACK (upstream never checks its ENOSYSed sysinfo call). Read /ctl/memory
# instead (the 0032 precedent); -1 on a miss, never a guess.
0034-pouch-sysconf-physpages.patch
# 0035: B-0 -- 0002's read backend never refilled f->buf, breaking the
# rpos[-1] pushback invariant: fscanf/scanf on a real FILE failed at the first
# pushed-back delimiter, and every getc was one syscall. Restores upstream's
# own no-readv refill arm, generalised to every request <= the buffer (small
# freads buffer too). Found by 0034's device pin.
0035-pouch-stdio-read-refill.patch
# 0036: B-0 audit r1 F2 -- tmpfile() never unlinked (raw SYS_unlinkat is a
# sentinel, result ignored), and an honest unlink-at-creation cannot work here:
# Stratum rejects I/O on an unlinked fid by design. tmpfile() is now
# delete-on-close: the name goes at fclose() and at a normal exit().
0036-pouch-tmpfile-delete-on-close.patch
# 0037: B-0 audit r1 F1+F6 -- sysconf(_SC_OPEN_MAX/_SC_CHILD_MAX), getloadavg,
# getdtablesize, ulimit, getdomainname all read an out-struct a sentinel-parked
# wrapper never filled (0034's defect, five more times; ualarm, the sixth, was
# round 2's); sysconf's /ctl reads stop being cancellation points.
0037-pouch-unchecked-sentinel-wrappers.patch
# 0038: B-0 audit r1 F4 -- the stdio backends handed a pouch SOCKET fd (a
# libc-side slot tag) to the kernel raw: fdopen(sock) never worked and fclose()
# stranded the slot (8 of them ends socket()). Map the tag as read/write/close
# do; ESPIPE for a seek. Pinned by pouch-hello-sockets' stdio + slot-count legs.
0038-pouch-stdio-socket-fds.patch
# 0039: B-0 audit r2 F2 -- a socket fd (0x40000000 | slot) does not fit an
# fd_set: FD_SET(sock) was a store 128 MiB past the set, in application code.
# FD_SET/FD_CLR/FD_ISSET now abort() on a descriptor that does not fit the set
# (glibc's __fdelt_chk: full width, against the set's own size); ppoll() goes
# through the tag-aware poll(). THE SERIES' FIRST PATCH INTO A PUBLIC HEADER
# (include/sys): the guard lives in the PORT's objects, so ports are rebuilt,
# not relinked. The real fix -- small-integer socket fds -- is owed.
0039-pouch-fdset-guard-ppoll-tag.patch
# 0040: B-0 audit r2 F9 -- O_APPEND was a one-time seek at open (0030), so a
# write after a seek landed mid-file. The opens now carry the kernel's OAPPEND
# omode bit (VIVARIUM 6.27; Stratum appends server side); the seek is kept for
# ftell() and the first "a+" read. NOT atomic against a concurrent appender
# (Stratum's write is stat-then-write).
0040-pouch-o-append-omode.patch
# 0041: B-0 audit r3 F1+F2 (libc half) -- poll() gives a CONNECTED AF_UNIX
# socket the stream-socket shape: a peer's orderly close is POLLIN|POLLHUP, not
# the kernel's pipe-like POLLHUP|POLLERR, so the "POLLIN? read; 0 = closed"
# loop every port has terminates. The kernel half (a client endpoint is
# pollable at all; every ring mutation walks the hook list) is ARCH 23.3. An
# ACCEPTED socket is untagged and not covered -- recorded in the header.
0041-pouch-poll-stream-socket-shape.patch
